Now you're ready to build and run your application. Open a terminal in your project directory and execute:

```shell
cargo run
```

This command will compile your Rust application and, upon successful compilation, will run it. You should see the timestamp being printed to the console every second. Additionally, you should see a tray icon appear (the appearance and behavior might slightly vary depending on your operating system). If you click or right-click on the tray icon (depending on your OS), you should see a context menu with a "Quit" option that allows you to exit the application.

