`import()` is a built-in JavaScript feature (Dynamic Imports) that allows you to load modules asynchronously. It returns a Promise that resolves to the module when the module is fetched and executed. You can use dynamic imports to separate parts of your application into separate chunks, reducing the initial loading time and improving performance.

Here's a simple example of how to use `import()` to load a module:

1. Create a file `example-module.js`:

```javascript
