The code you've posted here consists of an HTML5 canvas simple simulation of a solar system featuring the Sun and some planets. To improve it and model it in tune with local time and planet positions (although still significantly simplified), I can modify your starting code to include basic celestial mechanics angular adjustments.

Below is an improved version of your code that attempts to position the planets more accurately based on a very simplified model using the current time to generate a constant motion (not taking into account the elliptical nature of orbits, which would require resolving Kepler's equations):

```html
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Solar System Simulation with Labels</title>
    <style>
