To add buttons to a ListView in your Java Android Studio app, you can follow these steps:

1. Open your activity XML file (activity_main.xml) in the layout folder or any other XML file where you want to implement the ListView.
2. Add the ListView widget in the XML layout. For example:

```xml
<ListView
    android:id="@+id/list_view"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content" />
```

3. Create a new layout XML file for the ListView items (list_item.xml). This layout will represent each individual item in the ListView. For example:

```xml
<Button
    android:id="@+id/button"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:text="Button" />
```

4. In your Java code (MainActivity.java), create an ArrayAdapter to populate the ListView with the data and handle button clicks. For example:

```java
public class MainActivity extends AppCompatActivity {

    private ListView listView;
    private ArrayAdapter<String> adapter;
    private ArrayList<String> dataList;

    @Override
    protected void onCreate(Bundle savedInstanceState) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main);

        listView = findViewById(R.id.list_view);
        dataList = new ArrayList<>();
        adapter = new ArrayAdapter<>(this, R.layout.list_item, R.id.button, dataList);
        listView.setAdapter(adapter);

        // Add button click listener
        listView.setOnItemClickListener(new AdapterView.OnItemClickListener() {
            @Override
            public void onItemClick(AdapterView<?> parent, View view, int position, long id) {
                // Handle button click here
                Toast.makeText(MainActivity.this, "Button clicked at position: " + position, Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
            }
        });

        // Add data to the ListView
        dataList.add("Item 1");
        dataList.add("Item 2");
        dataList.add("Item 3");

        adapter.notifyDataSetChanged();
    }
}
